 34S  c  1975Va02: {+34}Cl{+m} was produced via the {+24}Mg({+12}C,pn) reaction 
 34S 2c  with a 35-MeV 12C beam from the Utrecht EN tandem accelerator. After   
 34S 3c  one hour of bombardment, the radioactivity was detected using a 100-cm2
 34S 4c  Ge(Li) detector and a 23|*28-cm2 NaI(Tl) detector for Compton          
 34S 5c  suppression. Measured E|g, I|g. Deduced levels, T{-1/2}, decay         
 34S 6c  branching ratios, and log {Ift} for {+34}Cl{+m} decay. Also briefly    
 34S 7c  reported {+34}Cl ground-state decay.                                   
 34S  c  Half-life measurements: 2006Ia05, 1983Ko22, 1976Wi08, 1973Ry01,        
 34S 2c  1972Ha82, 1965Eb01, 1965Fr06, 1961Ja22, 1960Ja12, 1958Mi85, 1954Kl36   
 34S  c  |b{++} spectrum measurement: 1956Gr07, 1953St42, 1951Ru24              
 34S  d  |b polarization measurement: M. Deutsch et al., Phys. Rev. 107, 1733   
 34S 2d  (1957).                                                                
 34S  cE TI$Upper limits for intensities are from 1975Va02. Upper limits for    
 34S 2cE unobserved peaks were taken as 4(N|*FWHM){+1/2}, where N is the number 
 34S 3cE of counts in the peak region and FWHM is estimated from neighboring    
 34S 4cE peaks. 1975Va02 states that the sum of the intensities of four allowed 
 34S 5cE branches is less than 1.2|*10{-4} of 34Cl ground-state decay.          
